    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10110" root="خدر" body-key="x">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُخَدَّرَةٌ</span></b>  (S, A, K) and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُخْدَرَةٌ</span></b>  and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَخْدُورَةٌ</span></b> 
(K) A girl <i>kept behind,</i> or <i>within, the curtain.</i>
(S, A, K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُخَدَّرٌ</span> (TA) and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَخْدُورٌ</span></b>  (A,
TA) <i>A curtained</i> [<i>vehicle of the kind called</i>]
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هَوْدَج</span>. (A, TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  [And hence,] ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَخْدُورٌ</span></b>  and
↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُخْدَرٌ</span></b>  (in some copies of the K and in the TA
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُخْدَرٌ</span> and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُخْدِرٌ</span></b> ) (tropical:)  A lion <i>concealed in his
lurking-place.</i> (K, TA.)

